    <dcterms:title>A Strange Discovery</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A_Strange_Discovery</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>E-text prepared by Suzanne Shell, Colin Cameron, Mary Meehan, Charles Franks, and the Online Distributed Proofreading Team</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"A Strange Discovery" by Charles Romyn Dake is a novel published in 1899 that serves as a sequel to Edgar Allan Poe's unfinished "The Narrative of Arthur Gordon Pym of Nantucket." An English narrator encounters Dirk Peters, the sole surviving companion from Poe's tale, forty-nine years after their original Antarctic voyage. On his deathbed, Peters reveals the missing conclusion: a warm polar civilization of Roman descendants, tragic romance, and heroic rescue amid volcanic peaks and mysterious white figures at the edge of the world. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 61.0 (8th &amp; 9th grade). Neither easy nor difficult to read.</pgterms:marc908>
